codex
The recursive circularity is now working: the final symbolic result is exactly “digits of the quotient, followed by the remainder digit.” The sole failed implication is that the destination-side `baseDigits(X,B)` was not expanded to that defining recurrence. I’m marking the recurrence explicitly as a backend simplification equation so it is available during the final implication check.
